<title>USA: Fed refrains from open market operations.</title>
<headline>Fed refrains from open market operations.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve refrained from open market operations on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Analysts had said the Fed was likely to stay out of the market, noting that the Federal funds rate was trading at 5-1/8 percent, below the Fed's 5-1/4 percent target for the overnight rate.</p>
<p>Analysts said the Fed could add permanent reserves to the banking system through a coupon pass later this week.</p>
<p>-- (( -- North American Treasury Desk 212-859-1679))</p>
